@startuml receipt-archive-states
title M-UM3: receipt evidence and archive fate (v0 design; no implementation claim)
hide empty description

state "Start receipt / execution evidence (§§4.7, 7)" as Receipt {
  state "No start receipt yet" as NoReceipt
  state "Root start receipt exists\nwritten before privilege drop / exec" as Recorded
  state "Stop absence confirmed\nresult receipt: remaining = 0" as Absent
  [*] --> NoReceipt
  NoReceipt --> Recorded : launcher: setsid, atomic root write\nthen clear groups / GID / UID / exec
  Recorded --> Recorded : launch with existing execution_id refuses\nexecution_already_started
  Recorded --> Recorded : helper stop refuses receipt / live identity mismatch\nor processes_remain / unknown observation
  Recorded --> Absent : helper exec.stop verifies active owned generation,\nreceipt + live identity; TERM / grace / KILL;\nno remaining processes incl. escaped descendants
  Absent --> Absent : receipt persistence/deletion rule unspecified\nno second-launch permission inferred
}
note right of Recorded
  Process: swarma-user-launcher, root until UID drop.
  Root-owned mode 0644 start receipt:
  execution_id, epoch, pid, start_time, boot_id, session_id.
  Location binds generation and execution_id (§7).
  Process: swarma-user-manager, root, owns exec.stop.
  Execution: curator-run -> harness under agent UID;
  dispatcher service UID owns execution lifetime.
  Unknown/failed observation is not known absence (§4.7).
  Post-receipt/pre-exec failure recovery and receipt deletion:
  unspecified in spec §§4.6, 7.
end note
note right of Absent
  Evidence condition, not a new persisted account state.
  Stop result receipt storage / retention: unspecified in spec §4.7.
  An existing start receipt still refuses another start (§7).
end note

state "Home fate after retiring commit and verified quiescence (§4.4.1)" as Archive {
  state "Home in quarantine\nsame-filesystem move; root-controlled" as Quarantined
  state "Archive retained\nroot-owned 0600 tar.zst" as Retained
  state "Home deleted" as Deleted
  state "Archive swept" as Swept
  [*] --> Quarantined : manager user.retire; account quiescent
  Quarantined --> Deleted : explicit home=delete\nno-follow descriptor walk
  Quarantined --> Deleted : home=archive exceeds max_per_archive\nafter exclusions; audit deletion
  Quarantined --> Retained : home=archive within bound\nlinks stored as links
  Retained --> Swept : archive.sweep: older than max_age\nthen oldest until max_total satisfied
}
note right of Quarantined
  Process: swarma-user-manager, root; installer/operator/dispatcher
  caller roles apply (§3); dispatcher only its own agents.
  Home content was account-owned; quarantine is root 0700 (§4.0).
  Journal recovery resumes retirement forward (§4.6).
  Quarantine disposal after archive: unspecified in spec §4.4.1.
  keep request refuses today: not in closed schema (§4.4.1).
  Operator-only keep/no-expiry is an OPEN owner choice, not a state.
end note
note right of Retained
  Manager owns archive and audit; root configuration owns retention policy.
  Configurable defaults: archive; max_age 7d; max_total 20GiB;
  max_per_archive 2GiB after configured exclusions (§4.4.1).
  Sweep at every retirement and daily root timer.
  Timer identity beyond root / retry on sweep failure:
  unspecified in spec §4.4.1.
end note
note "Defining spec: [[../spec/helper.md#7-the-launcher-swarma-user-launcher §7 start receipt]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#47-execstop §4.7 stop evidence]], [[../spec/helper.md#441-archive-policy §4.4.1 archive]].\nThese are two independent views, not a receipt-to-archive transition.\nCurrent repository: nothing implemented. v1 retains egress until account/group removal (§8).\nv2 grant grammar open (§9); SH1/SH2 receipt/archive variants unspecified in spec §§4.4.1, 7;\nSH2 host-role/ticket gate open (§14)." as Scope
Scope .. Receipt
Scope .. Archive
@enduml
